5a5eea4d-3d1c-5658-8171-517491bf7c77 {':db/ident': ':question.difficulty/easy'} Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.

$$
5{y}^{2}-y{e}^{-x}\frac{\text{d}y}{\text{d}x}=y,\,y\ne 0.
$$
SOLUTION A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as

$$
\frac{\text{d}y}{\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\,,
$$

where $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$

$$

$$

We have

$$
\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-y{e}^{-x}\frac{\text{d}y}{\text{d}x} & =y \\ -y{e}^{-x}\frac{\text{d}y}{\text{d}x}+5{y}^{2}-y & =0 \\ -y({e}^{-x}\frac{\text{d}y}{\text{d}x}-5y+1) & =0 \\ {e}^{-x}\frac{\text{d}y}{\text{d}x}-5y+1 & =0 \\ {e}^{x}({e}^{-x}\frac{\text{d}y}{\text{d}x}-5y+1) & =0 \\ \frac{\text{d}y}{\text{d}x}-5y{e}^{x}+{e}^{x} & =0 \\ \frac{\text{d}y}{\text{d}x}\,+\underbrace{(-5{e}^{x})}_{P(x)}y & =\underbrace{-{e}^{x}}_{Q(x)} \\ \frac{\text{d}y}{\text{d}x}-5{e}^{x}y & =-{e}^{x}\end{aligned}
$$

Now, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=-5{e}^{x}$ and $Q(x)=-{e}^{x}.$
